pred
User-defined predicate function object that defines the comparison criterion to be satisfied by successive elements in the ordering. This binary predicate takes two arguments and returns true
if the two arguments are in order and false
otherwise. This comparator function must impose a strict weak ordering on pairs of elements from the sequence. For more information, see Algorithms.
Remarks
The range referenced must be valid; all pointers must be dereferenceable and within the sequence the last position is reachable from the first by incrementation.
