Starting in C++11, a static
local variable initialization is guaranteed to be thread-safe. This feature is sometimes called magic statics. However, in a multithreaded application all subsequent assignments must be synchronized. The thread-safe static initialization feature can be disabled by using the /Zc:threadSafeInit-
flag to avoid taking a dependency on the CRT.
