is true.(t1.get().*f)(t2, ..., tN)
whenf
is a pointer to member function of classT
andstd::decay_t<decltype(t1)>
is a specialization ofstd::reference_wrapper
.((*t1).*f)(t2, ..., tN)
whenf
is a pointer to member function of classT
andt1
isn't one of the previous types.t1.*f
when N == 1 andf
is a pointer to member data of a classT
andt1
is an object of typeT
or a reference to an object of typeT
or a reference to an object of a type derived fromT
. That is, whenstd::is_base_of<T, std::decay_t<decltype(t1)>>::value
is true.t1.get().*f
when N == 1 andf
